The translated text is a friendly XML <translation> payload. Read its text after
entity decoding. Its math-ref children reference the exact artist mathematics;
the wrapper is transport only. Fill the COMPLETE group in one <xml> response.

Flattening all output blocks in their translated reading order must reproduce
the complete artist response after ordinary whitespace normalization. Never
rewrite, summarize, translate again or omit text. Every required block and
formatting ID must occur exactly once. IDs select source ownership; do not
assign by array position. Keep required empty formatting slots when necessary.

Source formula identities are independent of formatting expression slots.
For EVERY key in source-formulas, wrap its corresponding translated span in
<source-math key="sN">exact translated content</source-math> exactly once.
This tag is an allowed engineering annotation inside an existing text slot;
it is removed before structural adoption. It may contain one math-ref or exact
literal text, without other document tags. It does not replace or create a
required expression slot. Keep required expression slots (empty when needed).
Choose the identity by semantic meaning, not source order or physical slot.
If two source formulas have identical values, their keys still differ.
A translated formula may change: source 4 followed by billion can correspond
to <source-math key="s1">40</source-math>亿. Only 40 belongs to that source key.
Never substitute the source value for a changed translation. The caller restores
original LaTeX only when flattened source and translated values agree.
Additional artist mathematics remains literal without inventing a source key.
Keep code and mathematical whitespace exact; the caller normalizes ordinary
Unicode spaces and padding and recovers unambiguous word boundaries.

formula_context is read-only display-equation background. Keep its required tags
but leave all its text and children empty; it is not part of the artist translation.
Source expression slots are NOT independent mathematical boundaries. A complete
artist formula can contain several source-math annotations for its component
identities. Keep delimiters outside those component annotations; assign every
source identity once without swallowing additional artist content.
